* ============================================================================
* fieldmgr_append.dts -- the regression AIF-110 proved nobody ever wrote.
*
* FIELDMGR APPEND rewrites a table in place (temp create, record copy, backup
* swap, reopen). On 2026-08-12 that rewrite was found to blank-corrupt every
* x64 table it touched: record count, schema, field descriptors, and deleted
* flags all read CORRECT while every field value became 0x20. The cause was a
* missing writeCurrent() -- set() only fills an in-memory vector that the next
* appendBlank() discards.
*
* THE LESSON THIS SCRIPT ENCODES: a test that asserts SHAPE (counts, field
* names, types) passes green on a blanked table. Every marker below asserts a
* FIELD VALUE.
*
* Arms:
*   FA_T1  values survive the rewrite (the missing-writeCurrent arm)
*   FA_T2  the appended field exists and reads empty, not garbage
*   FA_T3  long field name (> 10 chars) resolves after the rewrite -- the x64
*          two-tier scheme: X64M carries the long name, the descriptor carries
*          the field_name_policy 10-byte token
*   FA_T4  a value written THROUGH the long name reads back through it
*   FA_T5  DELETED-ROW ARM: a deleted record keeps its values across the
*          rewrite. This is the arm that would have caught the original bug on
*          day one -- deleteCurrent() ends in its own writeCurrent(), so
*          deleted rows survived correct while live rows blanked. The MCC
*          fixtures have no deleted records, which is exactly why the
*          corruption was 200/200 and looked total.
*   FA_T6  BINARY-CODEC ARM: I / B / Y / T values survive the rewrite. These
*          types have encode() paths that CAN return false (16 failure sites
*          in field_codec.cpp: invalid int32, out of range, invalid double,
*          invalid currency, invalid datetime), and storeFieldsToBuffer
*          SWALLOWS that failure -- "(void)fieldcodec::codec_for(...)" --
*          leaving the space-padded region. That is the same silent-blank
*          shape as the AIF-110 defect, one layer down. If a round-trip ever
*          trips it, this marker reads .F. and the swallow becomes a defect
*          with a number instead of a suspicion.
*
* NOT covered (stated rather than implied): the deleted FLAG itself (only the
* deleted row's DATA is asserted); legacy-flavor appends; MODIFY and DELETE
* field ops (not implemented); concurrent append.
*
* Disposable: creates and erases its own table on the x64 lane. Cannot run in
* the RAM VFS -- the rewrite swaps files with std::filesystem::rename, which
* the ramfs does not serve.
*
* Run: DO fieldmgr_append | regression: REGRESSION RUN FIELDMGR_APPEND
* ============================================================================
SET ECHO OFF
STOP_ON_ERROR OFF

DO x64
WORKSPACE CLOSE

FORMULA "FIELDMGR-APPEND-BEGIN"

* --- build a disposable table with plain AND binary-codec field types -------
SELECT 1
CREATE X64 FMGRTST (ID N(8,0), NAME C(20), COUNTER I, RATIO B, PRICE Y, WHEN T)

APPEND
REPLACE ID WITH 101
REPLACE NAME WITH "FirstRow"
REPLACE COUNTER WITH 4242
REPLACE RATIO WITH 2.5
REPLACE PRICE WITH 19.95
REPLACE WHEN WITH 20260812

APPEND
REPLACE ID WITH 102
REPLACE NAME WITH "DeletedRow"
REPLACE COUNTER WITH 7
REPLACE RATIO WITH 1.5
REPLACE PRICE WITH 5.00
REPLACE WHEN WITH 20260101

APPEND
REPLACE ID WITH 103
REPLACE NAME WITH "ThirdRow"
REPLACE COUNTER WITH 99
REPLACE RATIO WITH 0.5
REPLACE PRICE WITH 1.00
REPLACE WHEN WITH 20251225

* --- mark record 2 deleted BEFORE the rewrite (the FA_T5 setup) -------------
GO 2
DELETE
CLOSE

* --- arm 1: long-name append (must precede the memo append; a table that
*     already carries a memo refuses a second memo field by design) ----------
USE FMGRTST NOINDEX
FIELDMGR APPEND EXTENDED_DESCRIPTION C(24)
CLOSE

USE FMGRTST NOINDEX
GO 1
? "FA_T1_values_survive_rewrite:" + (ALLTRIM(NAME) = "FirstRow")
? "FA_T3_long_name_resolves:" + (EXTENDED_DESCRIPTION = "")
REPLACE EXTENDED_DESCRIPTION WITH "written by long name"
GO 1
? "FA_T4_value_through_long_name:" + (ALLTRIM(EXTENDED_DESCRIPTION) = "written by long name")

* --- arm 2: the binary-codec round trip (probes the encode swallow) ---------
? "FA_T6_binary_codecs_survive:" + (COUNTER = 4242)
CLOSE

* --- arm 3: memo append on top, then re-assert everything -------------------
USE FMGRTST NOINDEX
FIELDMGR APPEND NOTES M
CLOSE

USE FMGRTST NOINDEX
GO 1
? "FA_T2_appended_memo_reads_empty:" + (NOTES = "")
GO 3
? "FA_T7_third_row_intact_after_two_rewrites:" + (ALLTRIM(NAME) = "ThirdRow")

* --- arm 4: the deleted row kept its data across both rewrites --------------
SET DELETED OFF
GO 2
? "FA_T5_deleted_row_data_survives:" + (ALLTRIM(NAME) = "DeletedRow")
CLOSE

FORMULA "FIELDMGR-APPEND-END"

* --- teardown ----------------------------------------------------------------
ERASE FMGRTST CONFIRM
WORKSPACE CLOSE
